  "slug": "salesforce-streaming-api-cometd-versus-pub-sub-case-consumers",
  "concept": "Salesforce Streaming API CometD versus Pub/Sub case consumers",
  "generated": "2026-11-12",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Salesforce Streaming API CometD versus Pub/Sub case consumers. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Definitions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Pub/Sub API is not a transport-only replacement for every legacy Streaming API subscription: it supports change data capture and high-volume platform events, but excludes PushTopic events, generic streaming events, and standard-volume platform events. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/supported-event-types.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2d20d01da536730158561b914d1cebbac7eb0bd97c8de790d98750db0ff2dad3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:abf2e18308f2f5cbb13d5a8508247b2228b72e82fd5eac915434bbfc99643915"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Streaming API pushes available events without client control of the delivered count. Pub/Sub API lets the consumer request a count based on its processing capacity, providing subscription flow control. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/pubsub-api-streaming-api-comparison.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2dc3d5bad4894ca544d7450f85420f8e1ddd54f2087aba2ce57c54111da5089d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2983c9f58f9e67dfb86eecdbf1844006f01cd75a30dd8498aca8f23325c287f3",
            "ev:52471e4b50c745fb5203268a7a33f2ba02f8a832970bb1a266741c5fb5fa4969"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pub/Sub CDC headers include changedFields and nulledFields that Streaming API omits; nulledFields, diffFields, and changedFields require further processing. Consumers must account for this header difference when migrating. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/cdc-event-diff-pubsub-cometd.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:eb70ac687b65bdbb36284b82241cf919764270d07ad213a08f10a7df38474d23",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1e70dbe9650ffce44d3c197f3751cf13c5e7a7f7bc15f55e3c01fa74993d8195"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pub/Sub documentation recommends saving replay_id from empty FetchResponse keepalives as well as processed events, because keepalives can advance the replay position and reduce seek time after reconnecting. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3bdf0b20c54556c98fd87529cf22392e8c2861a04daeb581e33d19fd56263809",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:01064851e29f67dae88b85a2e1e2263bce33ff6230bb3572f244950058e1e708",
            "ev:58a29361f77c19e2753220493ff184d3906d66a6bdb7bde2cbe65ce583e40e68"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Both APIs can replay retained CDC events after disconnection; Pub/Sub does not uniquely provide replay. The documented retention is three days for CDC and high-volume platform events, and a consumer cannot rely on events remaining after that window. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/using-streaming-api-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:599ff89e19cafc735480865906abf98ddfe7c2019442d10e697ef5989dfcd508",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:95c6e545948d8d444cf9f2dbbb792ca11b65006f3041442630ee79c033e6c2c0",
            "ev:9f8d3063dcb9e811a2bfda943b7acf00c01f5d35d454873868c05116858c3fb8",
            "ev:aff6081d7654502963ed86e676e988dbff4f43b57174f77cd989bfba07e792d9"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pub/Sub Subscribe still needs connection recovery: an error stops the long-lived connection, and the client must retry Subscribe to create a new connection. Changing the replay position requires a new Subscribe call because only the first FetchRequest replay option is honored. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:24c16548ba52b445f3a3e9eb17be8ec09d4e3a70f1f53d4af067c3974a0da0df",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2eb72010343895cb5aa732f8bef4f2bd6705b49a1589a2264cf027d6ffad08ed",
            "ev:68106c14f29fef0c2b59def9ef94910a3d1401366b890dfcbf102f1dd9306407"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Recovery options change names when migrating: Streaming API uses a specific replay ID, -1 for new events, and -2 for all retained events; Pub/Sub Subscribe uses CUSTOM with replay_id, LATEST, and EARLIEST respectively. Retrieving all retained events can slow performance in both APIs. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/using-streaming-api-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d8eaac84e830ff2992ac75c94136809b876e29ce3c68837419988477933684b8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:173f93e03a4a6e8bf0ddffdc3037e15cc9aed1b206ba5513e3069b2a2a1298f7",
            "ev:49b6c15ee2bc32059334640c3e4059c91ee8dd0a13e4741cba4edd0e2a62aab6"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In both APIs, the default subscription starts with new events rather than recovering the backlog. A reconnecting consumer should explicitly resume from a saved replay position when it needs missed events. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/using-streaming-api-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:081f50e40c9f2c9330d7b3276dda9604994898738c8ad71943b73440c991eae9",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:01064851e29f67dae88b85a2e1e2263bce33ff6230bb3572f244950058e1e708",
            "ev:74eea9b4a0e19377a48646152208c732125cee55c33239eb5464928cc3b94183"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pub/Sub change-event parsing also changes header and date handling: changedFields and nulledFields are included beyond the Streaming API header fields; nulledFields, diffFields, and changedFields require further processing; Pub/Sub dates use Epoch time rather than the Streaming API UTC representation. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/cdc-event-diff-pubsub-cometd.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:17029a32e3ada600b974a0f1725f8b378937076085ae86d7c5a619b2977d97d8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b8d7e742eb0b77b43596d460798249de7a90377c40641c4bf9321144d7557104"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For either consumer transport, persist replay positions rather than calculating the next position: replay IDs are opaque, need not be contiguous, and are used to recover retained events after disconnection. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6156ff5d262edf1f585d5f321c41b30ded98116409602899b0b22961467f40ea",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:15c6a156d12b27a3d0a3aff8ce446eef480235eb789698565dbc80f200b96797",
            "ev:81bfcbf8a59b2b681e6f016af187c9ebf8cd60e04a303c019ecc69dda2b59b55"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/using-streaming-api-durability.html"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Moving a Case change-event consumer from Streaming API to Pub/Sub API requires a wire-format change: CometD/Bayeux and JSON become gRPC/protocol buffers and an Apache Avro binary payload. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/pubsub-api-streaming-api-comparison.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8b8ea9d99b86b29a6ba106bd4c08ca7bfd09b46aa3128f25ac3cf962bacbd5d8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4dc54807cad041286dcc3abfb7b682dfc69bd4e14616f2c6c046901a44d52c9e",
            "ev:a7be8a3c0ab090758c743ca7ba5892ee37145a7bfc5df20310c7992fac14e817"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/cdc-event-diff-pubsub-cometd.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A migrated CDC parser must distinguish unchanged fields from cleared values: Streaming API omits null and unchanged record fields, whereas Pub/Sub API includes all record fields and represents unchanged and unpopulated fields as null. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/cdc-event-diff-pubsub-cometd.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:01bc18a8c15bbc2999ddaad3052f6a4094f42caba7a612e9dd8df2f79eefd431",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b3435e643c2a5f5cfc9e812dcc9be6012cd7564b3546c125d35aa57ddaef5939"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Streaming API documentation now specifies that, starting with API version 68.0, successful /meta/connect responses emit updated per-channel replay IDs in ext.replay[<channel>]. Comparisons claiming CometD never advances a cursor without event payloads must therefore be qualified by API version. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/using-streaming-api-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9dc3e0ad357c862642ef2614995ee029778da9b3f225d0f8c1a17fd2edd089fb",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:f50fcb05c830f47ae74534536a3c5cde5c0f9a8c29013e17f1362dc3d6a5bb9e"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A CometD GitHub issue reports missed Salesforce events while the client remained subscribed and long polling. The maintainer said the initial evidence could reflect bugs or application mistakes and requested connection-level and DEBUG evidence; the report does not establish a confirmed Salesforce or CometD defect. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/cometd/cometd/issues/1142",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:640e73a1ca0682d8141af75d41132da826ba3ba9485c36ab9e01674952485a6f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:05a41400c622a6a7fd90aceb6dcaa61d1c94deef099acec274dd8288205402cd",
            "ev:9af6899afe61bdffa1a265d8d5bfa083474d94068f23d581b64e403be1a301da"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Salesforce recommends Pub/Sub API for new external applications consuming platform events or change data capture events. Both Pub/Sub API and Streaming API can consume these event categories. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/cdc-event-diff-pubsub-cometd.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:327d12268d90c2003b54bdbda8c0bcf04eee5032f7c936da23f61888f60f78e5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:11be2d05b3659f8043d97b4afe32cbe7facc653c736192b1636dcd55ee74657c",
            "ev:f248a1827bdfce1498aae3b9a6e7fc7adfdca246d560fa8c8fb5a6b0eac5e44d"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/pubsub-api-streaming-api-comparison.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Switching transport does not extend the documented CDC retention window: Pub/Sub API and Streaming API both support replay of retained change events for 72 hours; Salesforce does not guarantee storage beyond that window. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a9e251d1797ca5f1cb5b64244c511c8a36e9a7ab495ebeafd772eadc99e7bca7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2d13731508ed396f39edba651582ea6f44ac6f6448b7641c73ce59fb08bcbb1f",
            "ev:64b8ab0686e627f64d6debba412ac38fe9e95216178f61304053c44e36b0db4c"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-streaming/guide/using-streaming-api-durability.html"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
